wifi_tether_configure_ssid_default: 'Nothing Phone (3a)' -> 'AndroidAP'

The default hotspot SSID broadcasts the device model to anyone scanning for
Wi-Fi while tethering is enabled. A generic name (AOSP default) removes that
identifier. Users can still rename it to anything.

Revert by restoring the 'Nothing Phone (3a)' string.
---
 rro_overlays/AsteroidsWifiOverlay/res/values/config.xml | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/rro_overlays/AsteroidsWifiOverlay/res/values/config.xml b/rro_overlays/AsteroidsWifiOverlay/res/values/config.xml
index 1ae212b..717c2b7 100644
--- a/rro_overlays/AsteroidsWifiOverlay/res/values/config.xml
+++ b/rro_overlays/AsteroidsWifiOverlay/res/values/config.xml
@@ -39,5 +39,8 @@
     <bool name="config_wifiSoftapIeee80211beSupported">false</bool>
 
     <!-- Do not translate. Default access point SSID used for tethering -->
-    <string translatable="false" name="wifi_tether_configure_ssid_default">Nothing Phone (3a)</string>
+    <!-- lenOS (OPTIONAL privacy): generic default tether SSID so enabling hotspot does
+         not broadcast the device model ("Nothing Phone (3a)"). AOSP default is "AndroidAP".
+         Revert by restoring the Nothing string. -->
+    <string translatable="false" name="wifi_tether_configure_ssid_default">AndroidAP</string>
 </resources>
